{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#131","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#131","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#131\",\"parent_revision\":\"11c656426ccb5c1715153b4e02ce508a774ed924cbc6e68b936ee4a3742a74d2\",\"root_revision\":\"11c656426ccb5c1715153b4e02ce508a774ed924cbc6e68b936ee4a3742a74d2\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`docs/screenshots/*.svg` are committed build outputs. There is no script that produces them and no CI check that they match the current rule set.\\n\\nThis is the root cause of two stale rows caught only by review, not by any gate:\\n\\n- an FM008 row surviving the rule's deletion (#105)\\n- an LK002 row surviving its deletion (#122)\\n\\n`README.md` links these, so the primary rule overview advertised rules `skilllint` could no longer list or run.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA `scripts/` regenerator covering all five screenshots, plus a CI staleness check so a rule change that invalidates a screenshot fails the build rather than shipping.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #105, #122 \u2014 the two stale rows this would have caught\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1bd408303e59da9cac41ae55bb0ceabc46806526f7fd10adb1745788ddbe6425\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP-51A\"}"}